SCOPE — what shipped (parity with the web source)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The web `WidgetRankedList` is a PURE presentational widget primitive (a shared widget building block): it
  takes `items: RankedItem[]` + optional `maxItems` / `compact` / `showBars` / `emptyMessage` / `emptyIcon`
  and renders an ordered leaderboard. Each RankedItem = a numeric `value` (the sort key + bar scale), an
  already-formatted `formattedValue` (the right-hand display string), a `label`, an optional `badge`
  (`{ text, variant: success|warning|error|neutral }`, mapped through the web `badgeVariantMap`: error ->
  danger), and an optional `barColor`. The render math: `limit = maxItems ?? (compact ? 3 : 5)`;
  `hideBars = compact || !showBars`; `visible = [...items].sort((a,b) => b.value - a.value).slice(0, limit)`;
  `maxValue = visible.reduce((m,i) => Math.max(m, i.value), 0)`; `barPct = maxValue > 0 ? value/maxValue*100
  : 0`. Its OWN render has exactly two branches:
    • list   (web `<ul>` of `<li>`: rank number `index+1`, an absolute background bar at `opacity-15` /
              width `barPct%`, the truncated label, the optional badge chip, the bold tabular value)
    • empty  (web `visible.length === 0 -> <EmptyState message="No data available" />`)

  There is NO fetch / React-Query / Promise in the source. Per the prompt's States section ("every state
  MUST render — no hidden surfaces": loading / empty / error / stale / offline) and the sibling LIST-primitive
  precedent WidgetEventFeed (0005), the native peer reproduces BOTH real web branches AND wraps them in the
  P4 host-lifecycle leaf contract so a dashboard-widget host can wire its query lifecycle without the
  primitive ever hiding:
    • loading — host query resolving -> skeleton ranked rows (rank chip + label line + value block)
    • empty   — the web `EmptyState` ("No data available"), never a blank box
    • error   — host query failed -> retryable error tile (web `QueryError` peer)
    • list    — the surface itself: the sorted + capped + ranked list (web body)
    • stale / offline — the orthogonal connectivity axis -> a freshness chip above the list with a one-shot
              auto-refresh on the stale transition
  These leaf states are the documented host-lifecycle WRAPPER, NOT invented web branches (the web body's two
  branches are reproduced verbatim inside the `.list` / `.empty` phases). The web `barColor` className
  passthrough is modeled as a theme-aware semantic `RankedBarTone` and the badge `variant` as `RankedBadgeTone`
  (-> shared `TSTone`) so no Tailwind class / raw hex enters the view (P1/S9), exactly as the sibling
  primitives map `valueColor` / `color` to tokens.

